   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1 Number of beneficiary smallholder women farmers with increased incomes from agricultural production (at least 30% of whom are poor and socially excluded women)
1.2: Number of beneficiary women with increased incomes from entrepreneurial (non-agricultural) activities (at least 30% of whom are poor and socially excluded women)
1.3: Number of beneficiary women having new or better employment (at least 30% of whom are poor and socially excluded women)
1.4: Number of women beneficiaries with increased information, strengthened capacities and skills to participate in the economy, including as farmers and entrepreneurs (at least 30% of whom are poor and socially excluded women)
1.5: # of proven cases of women beneficiaries who gain from joining networks/associations with the project&#x2019;s support
1.6: Share of budget allocations by target municipalities brokered through women&#x2019;s mobilization and/or meeting GRB principles
1.7 Number of women beneficiaries in a job-placement/internship arrangement with WEPs signatories 
1.1.1: Number of women with strengthened capacities and skills able to join the formal labour sector (at least 30% of whom are poor and socially excluded women)
1.1.2: Number of women with strengthened capacities and skills able to become farmers/entrepreneurs (at least 30% of whom are poor and socially excluded women)
1.2.1 Number of successful advocacy initiatives facilitated by women beneficiaries to overcome their socioeconomic challenges
1.2.2 Number of women beneficiaries who contributed to local planning and budgeting/GRB discussions aimed at addressing their socio-economic concerns (at least 30% of whom are poor and socially excluded women)
1.2.3 Number and share of municipalities that conducted one or more elements of GRB  (cumulative, as the project will continue working with 7 baseline target communities)
1.3.1: Number of private enterprises that signed the UNW/UN Global Compact WEPs with a focus on implementing gender-responsive corporate policies</narrative>
    </description>
